@startuml activity-workshop-day
!include _style.iuml
title Activity — the workshop day (UC40, UC41; grey: UC30, UC32–UC36, UC42)

|#EEF0F0|Workshop controller|
|#EEF0F0|Service advisor|
|Technician|
|System|
|#EEF0F0|Workshop controller|
start
#EEF0F0:Open the day's workload
(booked minutes per bay and technician); <<off>>
if (A technician is off or a bay is down?) then (yes)
  #EEF0F0:Move the affected jobs to another bay
  or technician, with a reason; <<off>>
  |System|
  #EEF0F0:Check the bay or technician that changes: active,
  right bay type, has the skill, on shift for the whole
  job; EXCLUDE has the last word
  (busy → 409 RESOURCE_BUSY); audit row "Moved: …"; <<off>>
else (no)
endif
|#EEF0F0|Service advisor|
#EEF0F0:Open the workshop day board
(bays as rows, jobs placed by time); <<off>>
#EEF0F0:Select a booking; <<off>>
note left
  "Has the vehicle arrived?" is decided at the desk.
  A CONFIRMED job may be started on any day, also
  before the booked one: the vehicle can arrive early
  (decided 27 Oct 2026, code review Q1).
end note
if (Has the vehicle arrived?) then (yes)
  #EEF0F0:Hand the vehicle to the
  assigned technician; <<off>>
  |Technician|
  :Open "Service requests", read the service,
  the checklist and the customer's note;
  if (Parts needed?) then (yes)
    #EEF0F0:Order parts for the job
    (parts staff order, receive and issue them); <<off>>
  else (no)
  endif
  :Start job;
  |System|
  :CONFIRMED → **IN_PROGRESS**;
  |Technician|
  :Do the work;
  :Show the customer the vehicle;
  :Customer agrees: finish job;
  |System|
  :IN_PROGRESS → **AWAITING_PAYMENT**
  (bay and technician freed; the customer
  sees "Awaiting payment");
  |Technician|
  :Customer pays at the desk;
  :"Customer has paid, close job";
  note right
    No bank integration in the demo: the payment
    is recorded by hand. Only the assigned technician
    (or a dealership admin, not in this version) may
    close a job, else 403.
  end note
  |System|
  :AWAITING_PAYMENT → **COMPLETED**
  (the customer sees "Finished");
else (no)
  |#EEF0F0|Service advisor|
  if (Start time passed and\nthe customer did not come?) then (yes)
    #EEF0F0:Mark no-show; <<off>>
    |System|
    #EEF0F0:CONFIRMED → **NO_SHOW**
    (bay and technician freed); <<off>>
  else (no: the booking must be dropped)
    |#EEF0F0|Service advisor|
    #EEF0F0:Cancel the booking (before work starts); <<off>>
    |System|
    #EEF0F0:CONFIRMED → **CANCELLED**
    (slot freed); <<off>>
  endif
endif
|System|
:Write the audit row (appointment_events),
log appointment.status_changed, count the metric;
note right
  Any other move (e.g. COMPLETED → IN_PROGRESS)
  → 409; a technician acting on someone else's
  job → 403. Nothing changes.
end note
stop

legend bottom right
  Blue: in this version    Solid grey: not in this version of the web app
  (service advisor, workshop controller, dealership admin, parts staff;
  the backend still has it). The customer can still cancel from My appointments.
endlegend
@enduml
